# Template for ~/.config/bugloop/gemini.env — the ONE line that carries the
# model credential. Copy it, put your own key in, and `chmod 600` the copy:
#
#   install -m 600 /dev/null ~/.config/bugloop/gemini.env
#   $EDITOR ~/.config/bugloop/gemini.env
#
# The operator loads it into the shell that runs `chia up`, and only there:
#
#   set -a; source ~/.config/bugloop/gemini.env; set +a
#
# `chia up` passes it to the llm workers with `docker run -e`; it is never put
# in a job's runtime_env, so it never reaches `chia job` output or the
# dashboard. No key belongs in this repository, ever.
#
# The key alone does not make the loop live: BUGLOOP_ALLOW_LIVE_MODEL=1 must
# also be set in that same shell, and a run without it refuses to build a model
# client at all.
# Put your key after the "=" below. Left empty, every stage refuses to build a
# model client and says so by name; a literal ${...} is refused the same way.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
